  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Heathcote’s name comes from Old English hēath, meaning “heather” or “wasteland,” and cote, meaning a cottage or shelter, hinting at a humble dwelling on open land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/heathcote-185041",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area that is now Heathcote began as farmland in Middlesex County before evolving into a suburban corridor thanks to its proximity to Princeton and New Brunswick.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/heathcote-185041",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Heathcote functions mainly as a residential enclave, drawing cultural and educational influence from nearby Rutgers University and the historic scholarly environment of Princeton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/heathcote-185041",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The community sits on a slope that drains south toward Heathcote Brook, a west‑flowing tributary of the Millstone River in the Raritan watershed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heathcote%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Route 1 cuts through the eastern side of Heathcote, linking the town northeast to New Brunswick and southwest to Trenton.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heathcote%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "County Route 522, known locally as Promenade Boulevard, runs east–west through Heathcote, connecting Routes 1 and 27 across the township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
